{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "05376bdf-efe9-5a4a-8a8b-61278b430c01",
    "name": "Incident Management – microservices",
    "description": "Every public endpoint of organization-, incident- and audit-service, plus organization's /internal API and the emails notification-service sends (checked in Mailpit), with assertions, so the collection is also the smoke test of ADR-0001 D12.\n\n**Configure:** use the *services-local* environment: one URL per service (organizationUrl, incidentUrl, auditUrl; there is no API gateway). Folder 2 calls organization's internal API ({{internalUrl}}). Users and demo ids are collection variables; change them under the collection's *Variables* tab.\n\n**Demo data** (fixed ids) comes from each service's `V…__demo_data.sql` migration. The demo incidents are only read, never changed, so the collection can run again and again.\n\n**Run all:** Postman *Run collection*, or `newman run IncidentManagement-services.postman_collection.json -e services-local.postman_environment.json`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "organizationUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8081",
      "description": "Overridden by the environment"
    },
    {
      "key": "incidentUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8082",
      "description": "Overridden by the environment"
    },
    {
      "key": "auditUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8083",
      "description": "Overridden by the environment"
    },
    {
      "key": "internalUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8081",
      "description": "organization-service, for folder 2 (its internal API)"
    },
    {
      "key": "mailpitUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8025",
      "description": "Mailpit, where notification-service sends the emails; overridden by the environment"
    },
    {
      "key": "ada",
      "value": "ada",
      "description": "Ada Admin, ADMIN, no team"
    },
    {
      "key": "alice",
      "value": "alice",
      "description": "Alice Lead: TEAM_LEAD of Database, RESPONDER in Network"
    },
    {
      "key": "bob",
      "value": "bob",
      "description": "Bob Reporter: no team, can only report and comment on his incidents"
    },
    {
      "key": "carol",
      "value": "carol",
      "description": "Carol Platform: TEAM_LEAD of Platform"
    },
    {
      "key": "dan",
      "value": "dan",
      "description": "Dan Dba: RESPONDER in Database"
    },
    {
      "key": "erin",
      "value": "erin",
      "description": "Erin Network: TEAM_LEAD of Network"
    },
    {
      "key": "bobId",
      "value": "20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003"
    },
    {
